  "term": "following behavior",
  "definition": "Following behavior is the way a driver adjusts speed, spacing, and braking while traveling behind another vehicle. In the packet, it is described as a key factor in traffic safety and energy use, because poor visibility and short following distance can increase speed fluctuations, stronger braking, and the risk of rear-end collisions.",
